rows.en:
That they were killed by Hanako-san is a lie.
What really happened was much crueler.
I'll tell you that story.{p}

She was locked in the girls' restroom on the third floor of the old school building.
In the second stall from the back of the girls' restroom.
Then they wedged a bar against the door from outside so she couldn't get out.{p}

...So this old school building will be torn down in just a few more days.
The old building held no particular nostalgia for me, yet it filled me with a strange melancholy.
I fell under the illusion that I had known it ever since it was brand new, freshly built.{p}

I took another look at the old school building.
For some reason, I found myself praying that it would never vanish.
If this is a dream, may I never wake from it...{p}

Suddenly my body seemed to float into the air, and then I was slammed into the ceiling with tremendous force.
I was completely upside down, as if gravity were coming from the ceiling.
The impact of being slammed must have made me hit my back hard.{p}

I saw it clearly.
The masked woman had taken off her mask and was looking up at me.
With a face shining like an angel's...{p}

And then she said,
"Seven... Seven, is it?
Were you really listening to what you were told? Liar..."{p}

I listened to her in silence.
I understood that they were victims.
But driving so many people to their deaths to drag them along... I wasn't so sure about that...{p}

Just then, a single ray of morning sun shone in.
The light fell on her face...
And then, for an instant, her face stirred and rippled.{p}

The clatter of the mask hitting the floor brought me back to my senses.
When the mask wobbled and fell, she was already gone.
She had vanished along with the butterflies.{p}

Had I seen an illusion, or had I been dreaming...?
Then I noticed a single butterfly fluttering around me, as if reluctant to leave.
The morning sun had already fully risen.{p}

"Uh, waaaaaaaaah☆"
My voice rang out through the old school building.
When my voice, echoing through the building, finally died away, a silence that seemed eternal returned.{p}

She looked up and gazed all around the sky.
As if she were someone who had forgotten to look at the sky for years...
I couldn't see her face behind the mask, but that was how it felt to me.{p}

...At that moment.
Her face suddenly began to crumble.
Like wax running in the heat, her face melted and flowed away.{p}

That's right.
There's no way I can be saved.
But you know, I'm not all alone anymore...{p}

"Iwashita, please..."
Had I lost my mind?
Answering a question like that.{p}

Iwashita... the one who had once tried to kill me.
Maybe I felt guilty toward Uchiyama.
Maybe that was why I chose Iwashita.{p}
